From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: a reservation refused past a hole is named a hole (Wine
 patch 1041)

A refused fixed reservation named the next mapping after it as the one holding the range, though that mapping began past the range's end and nothing was in it (GTAV's recompilation, #779, at 0x800000000). Such a range is now reported as one no mapping holds.
---
 ...-refused-past-a-hole-is-named-a-hole.patch | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1041-ntdll-a-reservation-refused-past-a-hole-is-named-a-hole.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1041-ntdll-a-reservation-refused-past-a-hole-is-named-a-hole.patch b/wine/patches/1041-ntdll-a-reservation-refused-past-a-hole-is-named-a-hole.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..babef45
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1041-ntdll-a-reservation-refused-past-a-hole-is-named-a-hole.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: A reservation refused past a hole is named a hole.
+
+The kernel's virtual query reports the next mapping at or after an
+address. When a fixed reservation was refused and that mapping begins
+past the request's end, nothing lies in the range: the kernel refused
+the reservation itself. The report named that later mapping as if it
+held the range (GTAV's recompilation: "reservation refused for
+800000000-840000000: 1000000000-1000110000 is "anon"", where 0x800000000
+was empty), which sent the reading the wrong way. It now says no mapping
+holds it.
+---
+ dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 7 +++++--
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+index 025b604..8f6f096 100644
+--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
++++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+@@ -886,7 +886,9 @@ static void *anon_mmap_tryfixed( void *start, size_t size, int prot, int flags )
+          * tells the two apart: a query reporting protection, flags and a
+          * name describes a mapping, while a cleared record covering the
+          * whole request describes a hole, meaning the reservation was
+-         * refused rather than blocked. This matters most at a fixed base,
++         * refused rather than blocked; so does a mapping the query found
++         * past the request's end (it reports the next mapping at or after
++         * start). This matters most at a fixed base,
+          * where a title's own image lying across a program's preferred base
+          * is indistinguishable from an exhausted address space. */
+         struct { void *start, *end; int64_t offset; int32_t protection, memory_type;
+@@ -895,7 +897,8 @@ static void *anon_mmap_tryfixed( void *start, size_t size, int prot, int flags )
+ 
+         memset( &info, 0, sizeof(info) );
+         query = sceKernelVirtualQuery( start, 1, &info, sizeof(info) );
+-        if (query || (!info.protection && !info.flags && (char *)info.end >= (char *)start + size))
++        if (query || (!info.protection && !info.flags && (char *)info.end >= (char *)start + size) ||
++            (char *)info.start >= (char *)start + size)
+             ERR( "reservation refused for %p-%p, which no mapping holds (query %d)\n",
+                  start, (char *)start + size, query );
+         else
